#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:5
#: e8365b2a99c54c5ab1fa8c2c3e77f5d7
msgid "Tuning Pivot Turns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:10
#: 9a961e82a2884e1981f720dbd93ad6bb
msgid "This page describes how to tune the \"pivot turn\" feature on a Rover (or boat) with :ref:`skid-steering <rover-motor-and-servo-configuration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:12
#: e022612d13524b1795fdb93aac19837c
msgid "A pivot turn involves the vehicle slowing or stopping, turning towards the destination and then continuing.  When enabled,these turns are only triggered in :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>`, :ref:`Guided <guided-mode>`, :ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>` or :ref:`SmartRTL <smartrtl-mode>` modes and only as a vehicle first starts towards the next waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:14
#: 0e3fb78b1bef4e6882f21abb9729496c
msgid "By default, smooth \"S-Curves\" are used all the autonomous modes including :ref:`Auto<auto-mode>`, :ref:`Guided<guided-mode>`, :ref:`RTL<rtl-mode>` and :ref:`SmartRTL<smartrtl-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:17
#: 56d347dd0169419bba814a0f4502ad15
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:19
#: e51d1205b45d406d8e3aa2dfb98f425a
msgid ":ref:`WP_PIVOT_ANGLE <WP_PIVOT_ANGLE>` holds the minimum angle error that will trigger a pivot turn.  By default, this value is \"0\" which disables Pivot Turn behavior and enables \"S-Curves\". For example when set to \"60\", a pivot turn will be triggered if the vehicle's heading is at least 60 degrees off from the next waypoint.  This parameter should normally not be set below 30 unless you wish to disable pivot-turns which can be done by setting this parameter to 0.  The vehicle will begin towards the next waypoints once its heading is within 10 degrees of the heading to the destination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:20
#: f2d6929cdcdb484792c9493df327adc1
msgid ":ref:`WP_PIVOT_RATE <WP_PIVOT_RATE>` holds the maximum turn rate of the vehicle (in degrees per second) during a pivot turn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:21
#: c92793b21c9740488e41597d1d92c11a
msgid ":ref:`ATC_STR_ANG_P <ATC_STR_ANG_P>` converts the vehicle's heading error into a desired turn rate.  Higher values lead to a more aggressive turn towards the destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:22
#: e9daf95a770a45e3bb60ca6371f5f1f9
msgid ":ref:`ATC_STR_RAT_MAX <ATC_STR_RAT_MAX>` limits the vehicle's maximum turn rate (in degrees per second) in all modes including during pivot turns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:23
#: ee185f30545f4c108b72a425f19fb7e6
msgid ":ref:`ATC_STR_ACC_MAX <ATC_STR_ACC_MAX>` limits the vehicle's maximum rotational acceleration (in deg/sec/sec) in all modes.  higher numbers lead to the vehicle getting up to its maximum turn rate more quickly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-pivot-turns.rst:24
#: 015d87d5adc34cf2ac26ef443a15dd03
msgid ":ref:`ATC_STR_DEC_MAX<ATC_STR_DEC_MAX>` sets the steering control angular deceleration maximum (in deg/s/s) that the autopilot will use when approaching a pivot turn to lessen overshoots. If set to 0, the :ref:`ATC_STR_ACC_MAX<ATC_STR_ACC_MAX>` value will be used."
msgstr ""

